    "body": "related #40697\r\n\r\n## Problem\r\n\r\n3p directory browsers can now handle `FileType directory` but there is no documented after-startup handoff for replacing `nvim.dir` (see point 1 in #40697 & linked issues).\r\n\r\nThis leaves plugin authors guessing on the roles of the global startup guard, augroup deletion, and the autocmd `FileType directory`.\r\n\r\n## Solution\r\n\r\n1. Document a canonical \"proper\" solution for overriding the directory buffers: deleting the `nvim.dir` augroup, handling `FileType directory` as the after-startup replacement path, and overriding keys.\r\n2. Clarify the role of what augroup deletion explicitly does (I felt it useful to implicitly delineate that it *does not* unload the plugin or remove mappings). \r\n3. Deal with [discussed annoyances](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/40458#issuecomment-4851360384) with the `-` mapping). Namely, avoid installing buffer-local `-` when `-` is alr mapped (matches global default behavior).",
    "closed_at": "2026-07-16T18:26:02Z",
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "_links": {
